WEBVTT

00:06.798 --> 00:08.425
[Usagi yells] Arisu!

00:08.508 --> 00:10.510
[panting]

00:14.889 --> 00:16.391
Arisu!

00:21.938 --> 00:23.523
[whimpers]

00:26.860 --> 00:29.696
[screams] Arisu!

00:30.488 --> 00:32.323
[theme music]

01:35.428 --> 01:36.429
Aguni.

01:39.516 --> 01:40.683
[Aguni] Hey, newbie.

01:43.895 --> 01:45.063
[Arisu] You're alive.

01:47.190 --> 01:48.358
Not by choice.

01:50.693 --> 01:52.070
Saw Niragi out there.

01:55.198 --> 01:56.825
So he survived too, huh?

02:02.163 --> 02:03.665
And what about the others?

02:06.584 --> 02:08.503
We broke off from Ann and Chishiya.

02:10.547 --> 02:12.382
Kuina went to track them down.

02:14.884 --> 02:16.302
Tatta didn't make it out.

02:19.347 --> 02:22.642
And me, I'm… going to look for Usagi.

02:24.727 --> 02:25.770
I see.

02:29.232 --> 02:30.483
Where are you going?

02:31.442 --> 02:34.779
I'm taking down the King of Spades.
We could use a hand.

02:35.530 --> 02:36.865
How are you gonna do that?

02:37.824 --> 02:39.534
[Aguni] He's just a man, isn't he?

02:40.034 --> 02:41.786
All men have weaknesses.

02:43.204 --> 02:44.497
[Arisu] He's too strong.

02:46.374 --> 02:47.292
Yeah.

02:48.042 --> 02:49.669
So it's perfect for me.

02:50.587 --> 02:53.798
One last battlefield
for those of us looking to die.

02:54.549 --> 02:55.842
A last battlefield?

02:55.925 --> 02:58.178
I should've died in the fire at the Beach.

02:59.762 --> 03:01.347
I've got nowhere to go…

03:02.223 --> 03:03.391
and nowhere to be.

03:06.269 --> 03:07.353
[Arisu sighs]

03:08.062 --> 03:09.898
Well, I don't have a death wish yet.

03:17.238 --> 03:18.907
Arisu, I have to ask.

03:20.742 --> 03:22.827
What are you living for, anyway?

03:23.786 --> 03:25.496
What's driving you, Arisu?

03:26.789 --> 03:29.375
Do you really wanna go back to our world?

03:29.459 --> 03:31.628
Or are you just running after a girl?

03:32.587 --> 03:34.172
[chuckles softly] Aguni.

03:36.591 --> 03:38.885
[chuckles] I don't need a reason to live.

03:44.807 --> 03:46.851
My purpose doesn't make a difference.

03:49.020 --> 03:50.438
Even if it's gone…

03:53.942 --> 03:55.610
Aguni, I need to keep living.

03:59.280 --> 04:01.366
That's a weak existence.

04:03.034 --> 04:04.827
Humans wanna live, don't they?

04:07.413 --> 04:08.414
I guess.

04:09.916 --> 04:11.209
I'm jealous, Arisu.

04:37.860 --> 04:39.362
[murmur of voices]

04:39.445 --> 04:40.947
- [girl 1] Wait a sec.
- [girl 2] Wow!

04:41.030 --> 04:43.324
- [girl 1] Your nails are so cute.
- [girl 2] Adorable!

04:43.408 --> 04:44.534
Where'd you get them done?

04:44.617 --> 04:47.870
- This place really close to the station.
- [boy 1] Yo, invite them!

04:47.954 --> 04:49.038
- [boy 2] No, you!
- Incoming.

04:49.122 --> 04:50.081
Hey, hey, hey.

04:51.916 --> 04:53.251
Barbecue on Sunday. Wanna come?

04:53.334 --> 04:55.295
- Barbecue!
- Barbecue?

04:55.378 --> 04:57.547
- You know it!
- Meat on the grill, ladies!

04:57.630 --> 05:00.091
We need memories
of our last high school summer.

05:00.174 --> 05:01.509
- Yeah!
- We can camp by the river.

05:01.592 --> 05:02.760
- I'm sorry.
- What do you say?

05:02.844 --> 05:05.888
That's the anniversary
of my mother's death.

05:05.972 --> 05:07.181
Oh. Brutal.

05:07.932 --> 05:09.726
We didn't know. Our bad.

05:10.476 --> 05:11.602
[scoffs]

05:11.686 --> 05:13.688
Yeah, that's because no one knows.

05:13.771 --> 05:15.898
Like I want people to hear that bitch died

05:15.982 --> 05:19.319
while on a trip with someone
she was cheating with. [laughs]

05:19.402 --> 05:23.489
Anyway, who the hell would wanna grill
meat outside when it's this fucking hot?

05:23.573 --> 05:25.700
- Wow, that was harsh.
- Seriously?

05:25.783 --> 05:27.744
They just want us to grill their meat.

05:28.369 --> 05:30.955
You think you got a shot with us?
What are you, idiots?

05:31.039 --> 05:33.458
- [all laughing]
- Aw, hey, I kinda feel bad.

05:33.541 --> 05:35.168
- Was that mean?
- You're terrible.

05:35.251 --> 05:36.711
Have fun with your meat!

05:39.255 --> 05:41.799
[girl 2] What? Don't you need
to go to archery club today?

05:41.883 --> 05:43.885
[girl 3] No, I don't feel like it.

05:43.968 --> 05:47.221
[girl 1] Oh, so apparently,
Meg broke up with her boyfriend.

05:47.305 --> 05:50.892
You're kidding. With Odaken?
They were, like, so in love.

05:50.975 --> 05:52.185
- Yeah.
- Yeah.

05:52.268 --> 05:53.936
[girl 3] Not so much in love.

05:55.355 --> 05:56.230
- Huh?
- Huh?

05:56.314 --> 05:58.858
- Do you know something?
- What are you talking about?

05:59.567 --> 06:01.402
He said he was over it.

06:01.486 --> 06:03.780
And then he said he was into me!

06:03.863 --> 06:05.365
- [gasps]
- [chuckles]

06:05.448 --> 06:07.700
Wait, did you sleep with Odaken?

06:07.784 --> 06:10.119
- So what? He came on to me first.
- Please!

06:10.203 --> 06:12.538
- Insane.
- You knew what you were doing.

06:12.622 --> 06:17.085
God, you really won't let anything
stand between you and a guy.

06:18.461 --> 06:19.629
Right? She can't help herself!

06:19.712 --> 06:22.131
- I can't compete with this--
- [explosion echoing]

06:22.215 --> 06:23.383
[gunfire]

06:24.342 --> 06:26.344
- Huh?
- [crackling]

06:26.427 --> 06:28.429
[distant screaming]

06:56.958 --> 07:00.002
PLAYERS, PLEASE GATHER
IN THE MIDDLE OF THE FIELD

07:00.086 --> 07:04.507
ONE PER PERSON

07:37.165 --> 07:40.126
PLEASE WAIT FOR THE GAME TO BEGIN
CURRENT TOTAL: 17 PARTICIPANTS

07:40.209 --> 07:41.878
Game? What is this?

07:44.755 --> 07:46.132
What's happening?

07:47.258 --> 07:49.051
Where did everyone go?

07:51.554 --> 07:53.431
You wanna survive, girl?

07:54.932 --> 07:57.143
Then you're gonna have to beat the game.

08:01.689 --> 08:04.734
- [PA chimes]
- [computer] Difficulty, Seven of Spades.

08:05.818 --> 08:08.070
Game, Boiling Death.

08:08.821 --> 08:10.615
Rules. Escape.

08:11.407 --> 08:15.119
The game ends
when the arena fully collapses.

08:21.042 --> 08:22.502
Fully collapses?

08:23.669 --> 08:25.671
[breathing unsteadily]

08:25.755 --> 08:27.465
[low rumbling]

08:28.758 --> 08:30.009
[gasps]

08:31.719 --> 08:33.804
[all talking in panic]

08:33.888 --> 08:35.806
[girl] What's… What's going on?

08:35.890 --> 08:38.100
[rumbling intensifying]

08:38.184 --> 08:39.769
[girl] Oh! What…

08:39.852 --> 08:41.229
[man gasping]

08:41.312 --> 08:45.149
This can't be happening.
I can't… I'm out of here!

08:45.233 --> 08:47.109
I don't wanna play!

08:56.827 --> 08:58.287
[man] Come on, run!

09:17.723 --> 09:19.725
[distant explosion]

09:20.351 --> 09:21.519
[groans softly]

09:21.602 --> 09:23.104
[wind gusting]

09:24.105 --> 09:25.439
[gasping]

09:31.237 --> 09:32.530
[groans]

09:33.948 --> 09:35.491
[whimpering]

09:36.909 --> 09:38.911
[distant, echoing shouts]

09:43.791 --> 09:45.876
[gasps]

09:46.669 --> 09:48.796
[screams]

09:51.674 --> 09:53.676
[crashing]

09:57.847 --> 09:59.557
[explosion]

09:59.640 --> 10:01.642
- [bubbling]
- [whimpering]

10:09.692 --> 10:10.651
[coughs]

10:10.735 --> 10:12.278
[whimpers and retches]

10:12.361 --> 10:13.613
[coughing]

10:13.696 --> 10:15.156
[crashing]

10:15.239 --> 10:18.326
[sobbing] It's hot! It's hot!

10:19.994 --> 10:20.953
[sobs]

10:22.079 --> 10:24.790
[wailing]

10:26.626 --> 10:28.628
[loud crashing]

10:29.587 --> 10:31.172
I gotta pull it out.

10:35.551 --> 10:37.053
[sobbing]

10:45.478 --> 10:47.480
[yelping]

10:50.274 --> 10:52.276
[screaming and crying]

10:59.200 --> 11:00.910
[explosion]

11:05.373 --> 11:07.375
- [loud crashing]
- [continues sobbing]

11:13.714 --> 11:15.549
- [rattling]
- [sobbing fades]

11:15.633 --> 11:17.760
[explosion]

11:25.810 --> 11:27.186
[grunting]

11:32.983 --> 11:34.235
[sobbing]

11:34.318 --> 11:36.320
[explosion, rubble crashing]

11:37.613 --> 11:39.323
[moaning]

11:52.086 --> 11:54.338
- [explosion]
- [groans] You can do it!

11:56.882 --> 11:58.884
[panting]

12:06.600 --> 12:08.602
[explosion]

12:11.814 --> 12:13.524
[groans]

12:13.607 --> 12:17.570
I know that I wasn't the best person
before. I know!

12:17.653 --> 12:23.075
[groans] Someone sent me to this nightmare
because I wasn't good?

12:23.159 --> 12:24.994
[growls]

12:25.077 --> 12:27.705
[shrieks] I don't deserve
to die like this!

12:27.788 --> 12:29.749
- [explosion]
- [crying]

12:29.832 --> 12:32.418
[growls] It's all that bitch's fault…

12:34.003 --> 12:36.005
[sobbing]

12:39.967 --> 12:41.635
[coughing]

12:59.612 --> 13:01.447
[man] This isn't who you are.

13:10.080 --> 13:11.123
Takeru.

13:27.389 --> 13:28.682
Why are you here?

13:30.518 --> 13:32.812
You think working with them will help you?

13:37.399 --> 13:39.652
You even bothered to save Arisu.

13:40.778 --> 13:43.072
Maybe you've got death on your mind?

13:44.365 --> 13:47.201
You're trying to make up for all those
people you killed

13:47.284 --> 13:48.911
back at the Beach, aren't you?

13:51.121 --> 13:55.501
The King of Spades isn't like you or me.
He's a mighty warrior.

13:57.211 --> 13:59.463
You don't deserve to die like a hero.

14:07.263 --> 14:09.348
You wanna die so damn bad?

14:11.809 --> 14:14.144
You should put a bullet
through your skull.

14:33.372 --> 14:34.540
[Arisu] Aguni.

14:35.666 --> 14:37.209
We have to stop this.

14:38.878 --> 14:40.921
No more innocent people have to die.

14:41.797 --> 14:43.340
Too many have already.

14:46.719 --> 14:47.970
All right, I get it.

14:49.471 --> 14:50.723
Please just go now.

15:11.785 --> 15:13.787
[shuffling]

15:33.182 --> 15:34.516
Are you awake?

15:40.397 --> 15:41.732
[scoffs]

15:42.441 --> 15:43.943
Hey, are you a virgin or what?

15:44.526 --> 15:45.444
No!

15:45.527 --> 15:47.237
[laughs]

15:59.041 --> 16:00.209
All right…

16:01.293 --> 16:03.462
Um, which way to the city?

16:03.963 --> 16:06.382
[girl] Huh? You're leaving already?

16:06.882 --> 16:08.300
I'm looking for someone.

16:10.219 --> 16:12.012
[girl] Like a girl someone, right?

16:12.972 --> 16:13.806
Usagi?

16:14.598 --> 16:15.891
You shouldn't eavesdrop.

16:17.142 --> 16:19.269
[girl] Hmm! [laughs]

16:24.984 --> 16:26.694
Do you think I'm cuter than her?

16:27.361 --> 16:28.445
What?

16:31.615 --> 16:33.033
That sounds like a yes.

16:33.617 --> 16:36.203
- No.
- [laughs] Are you blushing?

16:36.286 --> 16:37.371
No, I'm not.

16:46.922 --> 16:48.632
You seem nice enough.

16:49.675 --> 16:52.052
- Huh?
- And you're pretty cute too…

16:52.136 --> 16:54.096
- All right, let's do it.
- Whoa, hang on! Hey!

16:54.179 --> 16:55.180
[grunts]

16:55.264 --> 16:58.851
We have to live in a world where we don't
know if we'll survive the day, you know?

16:58.934 --> 17:01.437
- And besides, it's been so long…
- Get off me !

17:01.520 --> 17:02.438
- Gah!
- Come on!

17:02.521 --> 17:03.731
- [both grunt]
- [leaves rustling]

17:04.565 --> 17:05.607
[girl gasps]

17:07.443 --> 17:08.902
[gasps] Uh…

17:08.986 --> 17:11.572
This… This isn't what it looks like.
It's nothing!

17:11.655 --> 17:13.866
Don't look at me like that! You…

17:13.949 --> 17:16.035
You already said no, so…

17:16.702 --> 17:18.495
We're on the move. Get up.

17:19.163 --> 17:23.042
What? I'm not going with you.
I'm going to look for Usagi.

17:23.125 --> 17:25.544
You should be worried
about yourself right now.

17:26.837 --> 17:30.340
As soon as he gets us in his sights,
he's gonna attack.

17:30.424 --> 17:32.801
He might even be tracking us here already.

17:33.302 --> 17:34.136
I don't know.

17:34.636 --> 17:36.805
But we definitely have to keep moving.

17:37.431 --> 17:40.142
We'll lead him up
into the mountains somewhere.

17:40.225 --> 17:41.477
Then we'll strike.

17:43.145 --> 17:45.689
More people means more chances. Here.

17:48.692 --> 17:49.860
Hey, wait!

17:51.862 --> 17:54.198
Oh my God. He's so cool.

17:54.281 --> 17:55.199
[Arisu sighs]

17:59.578 --> 18:01.663
[Aguni] The King of Spades
is always on the move,

18:01.747 --> 18:03.749
looking for more players to kill.

18:05.084 --> 18:07.753
[girl] But it's not random, right?
It feels targeted.

18:07.836 --> 18:09.797
[Aguni] I bet he's keeping tabs on us.

18:10.672 --> 18:12.800
We'll find a good spot to ambush him.

18:19.098 --> 18:21.225
The King of Spades is never going to stop.

18:22.392 --> 18:23.936
He's already killed so many.

18:25.229 --> 18:28.482
I figured we'd be safe
if we stayed out here in the woods,

18:29.775 --> 18:31.276
but that didn't stop him.

18:32.736 --> 18:33.946
[sighs]

18:35.155 --> 18:38.951
The compass is saying
we should be near Kichijoji Station.

18:39.910 --> 18:40.953
You sure?

18:49.461 --> 18:51.463
[wind rustling through leaves]

18:54.258 --> 18:56.260
[metal tapping]

19:04.101 --> 19:05.561
[tapping stops]

19:11.859 --> 19:14.486
[Arisu] Killed himself
before his visa could run out.

19:15.487 --> 19:19.283
That son of a bitch didn't even fight.
He just took the coward's way out.

19:20.200 --> 19:22.578
In a world like this,
can you really blame him?

19:25.122 --> 19:27.541
All I know is I'll never make that choice.

19:29.710 --> 19:32.171
You ever lose someone you were close to
in a game?

19:35.007 --> 19:36.175
No, I haven't.

19:38.510 --> 19:39.720
What I lost…

19:41.930 --> 19:44.349
was an important piece of who I was.

19:50.564 --> 19:52.566
[whimpering]

19:53.233 --> 19:55.235
[explosion]

19:58.071 --> 20:00.032
[straining and gasping]

20:08.582 --> 20:10.584
[sobbing]

20:17.883 --> 20:19.551
[explosion]

20:25.057 --> 20:27.059
[whimpering]

20:33.815 --> 20:35.484
[explosion]

20:38.362 --> 20:39.613
[woman] Akane.

20:45.494 --> 20:47.496
[Akane] Mom? [gasps]

20:48.372 --> 20:49.414
[gasps]

20:51.041 --> 20:52.918
What the hell are you doing here?

21:03.929 --> 21:05.389
[mother shouts] Akane!

21:11.061 --> 21:12.187
[sobs]

21:17.442 --> 21:18.694
Come to me.

21:20.028 --> 21:22.155
[rumbling and crashing]

21:22.239 --> 21:23.573
[whimpering]

21:28.537 --> 21:30.539
Can I trust you, Mom? Huh?

21:35.419 --> 21:36.545
[sobbing]

21:44.386 --> 21:46.179
[screams]

21:53.395 --> 21:55.397
[gasping]

22:02.612 --> 22:03.864
It's not hot.

22:05.073 --> 22:06.366
[coughing]

22:12.456 --> 22:15.042
[Akane] I was the only survivor
of my first game.

22:18.045 --> 22:21.965
My mom, that cheating bitch,
her ghost saved my life.

22:31.933 --> 22:33.935
[whimpering]

22:44.112 --> 22:45.113
[gasps]

22:47.115 --> 22:48.658
The color's getting weird.

22:48.742 --> 22:49.785
[shivering]

22:50.660 --> 22:53.080
[gasps] I'm gonna die.

22:53.163 --> 22:54.623
[gasps] It's gonna kill me.

22:56.875 --> 22:59.503
[man] That is some advanced gangrene.

23:04.591 --> 23:05.801
[sighs]

23:08.387 --> 23:10.389
That leg has to go.

23:10.472 --> 23:12.224
At least, if you wanna survive.

23:13.767 --> 23:15.102
You a doctor?

23:15.185 --> 23:16.728
[breathing shakily]

23:16.812 --> 23:17.938
Can you help me, then?

23:18.730 --> 23:20.399
What, help you for free?

23:20.482 --> 23:23.110
Do you want money? How can I pay?

23:23.902 --> 23:26.405
[laughs] Hah! Adorable.

23:27.155 --> 23:29.866
Like I have any use for money here.

23:30.867 --> 23:31.993
Come on.

23:47.592 --> 23:48.802
Okay, then…

23:53.682 --> 23:55.600
Just do something for my leg!

24:02.399 --> 24:04.067
Aah!

24:16.496 --> 24:19.166
I owe a debt
to the me who survived that day.

24:20.792 --> 24:22.502
I'm here because of what she did.

24:23.253 --> 24:25.464
So I'll survive, no matter what the cost.

24:27.466 --> 24:29.509
I'm never gonna take the easy way out.

24:31.428 --> 24:32.846
I have to keep living.

24:40.645 --> 24:42.647
[soft rainfall]

24:53.575 --> 24:54.868
[sighs]

25:21.061 --> 25:22.229
[sighs]

25:40.038 --> 25:41.248
[retches]

25:41.957 --> 25:43.416
[gasps]

25:54.636 --> 25:56.179
[gasps]

26:08.275 --> 26:10.235
We already looked. There's nothing.

26:21.580 --> 26:22.706
[Usagi sighs]

26:22.789 --> 26:24.749
If you want, help yourself.

26:33.675 --> 26:34.759
Thank you.

26:37.846 --> 26:38.847
He's yours?

26:42.601 --> 26:45.520
I found him all alone
while I was playing tag.

26:47.897 --> 26:49.190
And your parents?

26:55.488 --> 26:56.615
[soft thud]

26:57.657 --> 26:59.200
I think they might be dead.

27:00.160 --> 27:02.746
He doesn't have much time
left on his visa.

27:02.829 --> 27:04.748
I couldn't leave him alone.

27:05.915 --> 27:07.542
[sighs] In that case,

27:08.835 --> 27:10.837
even if he makes it back to our world,

27:12.339 --> 27:13.548
it'll be hard.

27:16.968 --> 27:18.637
His life won't be easy.

27:21.681 --> 27:22.515
But

27:23.475 --> 27:29.230
I have to believe that his parents want
their son to live and make it back safe.

27:31.608 --> 27:34.152
They must want him
to find happiness there.

27:35.779 --> 27:36.905
I know it.

27:55.799 --> 27:57.801
[birdsong]

28:00.595 --> 28:01.638
[man] Yuzuha.

28:02.347 --> 28:03.682
Yeah?

28:03.765 --> 28:06.184
If something happens and I disappear,

28:07.310 --> 28:09.479
promise you won't be sad.

28:10.480 --> 28:12.107
What are you saying?

28:12.190 --> 28:13.817
It's what I want.

28:13.900 --> 28:16.361
It's my dream to die in the mountains.

28:17.112 --> 28:18.613
[Usagi] Don't say that.

28:20.281 --> 28:22.200
I don't wanna die like… [sighs]

28:22.283 --> 28:25.537
[mimics old man]
…an old man in the hospital.

28:25.620 --> 28:26.663
[laughs]

28:27.997 --> 28:29.374
[both laughing]

28:30.291 --> 28:32.460
Ah, if the mountains kill me,

28:33.128 --> 28:35.672
then that's just proof I lived well.

28:37.215 --> 28:39.259
And so if that happened,

28:39.342 --> 28:42.470
I want you to live
as full a life as possible.

28:42.554 --> 28:43.805
To go on.

29:44.407 --> 29:46.993
We must be around Yokohama right now.

29:53.124 --> 29:54.876
[low whirring]

29:55.502 --> 29:57.504
[whirring growing louder]

30:06.221 --> 30:08.431
Is this forest ever going to end?

30:09.349 --> 30:11.351
[distant whooshing]

30:22.821 --> 30:24.823
[insect buzzing]

30:59.607 --> 31:01.276
[tense, dramatic music]

31:02.402 --> 31:04.404
[Aguni] We'll lure him here.

31:05.697 --> 31:06.531
[Arisu] Here?

31:07.615 --> 31:08.700
This is a cliff.

31:09.617 --> 31:11.077
Nobody asked you.

31:20.169 --> 31:21.546
A smoke bomb?

31:21.629 --> 31:23.840
The traps warn us of incoming attacks.

31:24.632 --> 31:26.676
We'll be alerted by them, even at night.

31:27.635 --> 31:29.637
It's too bad we don't have any grenades.

31:30.638 --> 31:32.140
Set up all the wires we have.

31:33.600 --> 31:34.767
Why just use wire?

31:35.560 --> 31:38.062
A trap doesn't have to be real
to be effective.

31:38.146 --> 31:41.107
As long as it makes the enemy go
where you want them to go.

31:42.775 --> 31:43.860
You know a lot.

31:44.444 --> 31:46.362
- Sure do.
- I taught her.

31:47.822 --> 31:49.490
You keep watch at the tent.

32:09.636 --> 32:11.012
[rustling]

32:11.095 --> 32:12.263
[gasps]

32:12.347 --> 32:13.932
[wings fluttering]

32:21.397 --> 32:22.607
[sighs]

32:26.527 --> 32:27.695
[soft rustling]

33:49.235 --> 33:51.154
[panicked gasping]

34:23.978 --> 34:25.605
Was I bait for you?

34:25.688 --> 34:27.231
You have a talent for it.

34:30.818 --> 34:31.903
He invincible?

34:31.986 --> 34:33.613
[Aguni] It's a bulletproof vest.

34:33.696 --> 34:35.865
My guess is he's a mercenary.

34:35.948 --> 34:38.618
We'll cover each other
while we lead him to the cliff.

34:40.244 --> 34:41.287
Go.

34:52.924 --> 34:54.342
[yelps]

35:00.473 --> 35:02.308
[panting]

35:05.019 --> 35:05.978
[yelps]

35:21.994 --> 35:23.121
[gunshots]

35:26.791 --> 35:27.834
Arisu! Run!

35:29.794 --> 35:30.962
[gasps]

35:31.546 --> 35:32.713
[yelps]

35:32.797 --> 35:34.298
[screams]

35:35.174 --> 35:36.342
Arisu!

36:18.176 --> 36:19.218
Aguni!

36:43.326 --> 36:45.036
[breathing shakily]

37:12.939 --> 37:14.482
[grunting]

37:41.634 --> 37:43.636
[insects chirping]

38:07.702 --> 38:09.704
[bird calling]

38:22.383 --> 38:24.385
[quiet, wistful music]

38:39.483 --> 38:40.568
Usagi!

38:48.826 --> 38:49.952
Ah!

38:50.036 --> 38:51.329
[yelps]

38:55.082 --> 38:56.334
I'm sorry.

39:00.755 --> 39:01.839
[sighs]

39:30.493 --> 39:31.994
[sighs]

39:43.339 --> 39:44.632
[grunts]

40:02.441 --> 40:05.361
- [man 1 yells] That's it!
- [man 2] Yeah! We did it!

40:06.612 --> 40:08.406
- [laughter]
- [man 3] All right!

40:08.489 --> 40:10.783
- [man 4] All right! We did it!
- [woman] Yeah!

40:10.866 --> 40:13.577
[man 1] Yeah! Yeah!

40:15.079 --> 40:15.913
[man 2] We won this!

40:15.996 --> 40:17.164
Run!

40:17.873 --> 40:19.500
- We got this!
- I'm done!

40:19.667 --> 40:21.210
- I can't do it.
- Keep going!

40:21.293 --> 40:22.837
- [groaning]
- [Arisu] Usagi!

40:27.258 --> 40:28.676
Usagi!

40:28.759 --> 40:30.511
- [man] Keep moving.
- [woman] Yeah!

40:41.313 --> 40:42.565
[sighs]

40:43.274 --> 40:44.191
[grunts]

40:49.155 --> 40:50.865
No blaze of glory for me…

41:04.378 --> 41:05.421
Go.

41:12.052 --> 41:13.554
[yells] Get outta here!

41:17.224 --> 41:18.476
Aguni?

41:19.351 --> 41:20.227
[gasps]

41:22.897 --> 41:25.191
- [drops sticks]
- [gasping]

41:25.274 --> 41:27.026
- [grunts]
- [sobs]

41:35.326 --> 41:37.495
You're all right! [sobbing]

41:43.375 --> 41:45.377
[continues crying]

41:57.681 --> 41:59.433
[inspiring music]

42:18.744 --> 42:20.746
[insects chirping]

42:20.829 --> 42:22.831
[music swells]

42:54.572 --> 42:56.907
[computer over PA]
Difficulty, Jack of Spades.

43:01.662 --> 43:03.038
[man yelps]

43:38.699 --> 43:41.368
[sighs] I gotta hand it
to these face card games.

43:41.452 --> 43:43.245
They're not messing around.

43:45.205 --> 43:47.124
[sighing] Ow, that's not good.

43:56.342 --> 43:58.344
- [pours water]
- [groans]

44:01.972 --> 44:03.974
[gasping]

44:15.903 --> 44:17.738
They won't beat me.

44:35.547 --> 44:37.132
[wind whistling]

44:41.011 --> 44:42.513
[panting]

45:07.913 --> 45:09.707
[gasping]

45:19.842 --> 45:21.802
This isn't the world I know.

45:27.516 --> 45:28.976
[gasps]

45:55.043 --> 45:56.128
[boy] I'm not going.

46:00.215 --> 46:01.633
Do you want to die?

46:05.637 --> 46:06.638
No?

46:07.306 --> 46:09.057
Then let's win it together.

46:10.684 --> 46:12.728
But what's going to happen to us?

46:18.358 --> 46:19.401
If we win…

46:21.236 --> 46:22.905
we get to go back home.

46:26.575 --> 46:28.202
They're not there anymore.

46:30.078 --> 46:31.955
Mom and Dad are both gone.

46:37.002 --> 46:38.045
I get it.

46:39.505 --> 46:42.925
What is it that you think your parents
would want you to do, Kota?

46:46.804 --> 46:48.597
They'd want me to come home.

46:50.933 --> 46:52.059
Then let's go.

46:59.608 --> 47:00.567
[exhales]

47:06.490 --> 47:07.616
[bell pings]

47:10.118 --> 47:12.120
[machinery clanking rhythmically]

47:22.548 --> 47:23.715
[Usagi gasps]

47:42.442 --> 47:43.944
And how old are you, kid?

47:44.903 --> 47:45.863
[Kota] I'm ten.

47:48.031 --> 47:49.199
You're a good kid.

47:54.246 --> 47:57.082
This is a Spade game,
and you can't have a kid here.

47:57.958 --> 48:00.460
If he weighs us down,
I'll do what I have to.

48:02.087 --> 48:03.213
So don't blame me.

48:07.926 --> 48:10.804
- [sighs]
- [Arisu] Usagi has what it takes to win.

48:10.888 --> 48:11.930
[gasps]

48:17.269 --> 48:19.187
Arisu. [gasps]

48:19.897 --> 48:20.981
Usagi.

48:28.447 --> 48:30.282
I knew you'd still be alive.

48:31.867 --> 48:32.868
Me too.

48:34.369 --> 48:36.371
But how did you know I'd be here?

48:37.623 --> 48:39.583
I knew you'd try a physical game.

48:40.375 --> 48:43.837
All that's left is the Queen of Spades
and the King.

48:57.851 --> 48:58.936
[Usagi sighs]

49:15.327 --> 49:16.745
[Usagi gasps]

49:16.828 --> 49:17.913
And this is Kota.

49:18.622 --> 49:20.332
His visa runs out today.

49:21.291 --> 49:22.542
So you brought him here?

49:23.669 --> 49:27.089
I figured that
I could help him in a Spade game.

49:30.175 --> 49:31.051
[gasps]

49:31.134 --> 49:32.886
- [murmuring]
- [man] What's going on?

49:35.514 --> 49:37.349
[computer over PA] Game, Checkmate.

49:38.058 --> 49:39.267
[man] Checkmate?

49:40.978 --> 49:45.899
Today, the Queen Team will face off
against you, the Challenger Team.

49:48.110 --> 49:49.778
[woman] Welcome, Challenger Team.

49:49.861 --> 49:53.031
Welcome to the arena
of beautiful bodies in motion.

49:53.949 --> 49:56.493
I am the Queen of Spades.

49:57.577 --> 50:01.248
The Queen Team is made up of four members,
including myself.

50:01.331 --> 50:04.251
Your Challenger Team has 16 members.

50:04.334 --> 50:06.378
Do you think they're citizens as well?

50:07.421 --> 50:09.006
[woman] Each team will have a King.

50:09.089 --> 50:10.716
Don't worry, I'll choose.

50:11.550 --> 50:13.218
The Queen Team's King

50:14.344 --> 50:15.387
is me.

50:16.555 --> 50:19.808
Now, I'm looking
for a good Challenger King.

50:21.018 --> 50:22.352
Who's it gonna be?

50:25.397 --> 50:26.398
Oh.

50:28.233 --> 50:29.526
I choose him.

50:40.078 --> 50:42.080
[breathing shakily]

50:49.087 --> 50:50.505
[computer] Game rules.

50:52.299 --> 50:56.928
The teams will alternate taking turns
for a total of 16 rounds.

50:57.012 --> 50:58.930
During the Queen Team's turn,

50:59.014 --> 51:03.852
the Queen Team's players
will chase the Challenger Team's players.

51:03.935 --> 51:07.147
If the button on a player's back
is pressed,

51:07.230 --> 51:10.025
the button's light
will turn from blue to red,

51:10.108 --> 51:11.693
the Queen Team's color.

51:12.652 --> 51:17.282
That player may not move
for the remainder of that round.

51:17.365 --> 51:18.992
Starting on the following round,

51:19.076 --> 51:23.080
that player will now be considered
a member of the Queen Team.

51:23.914 --> 51:27.959
The King, however,
is not allowed to change teams.

51:29.753 --> 51:33.924
The opposite will occur
during the Challenger Team's turns.

51:34.007 --> 51:37.427
Each turn will last no more
than five minutes.

51:37.511 --> 51:41.515
After the end of 16 rounds
of alternating turns,

51:41.598 --> 51:44.518
the team with the most members wins.

51:45.227 --> 51:48.146
The members of the losing team,
including the King,

51:48.230 --> 51:49.981
will all die.

51:50.774 --> 51:52.275
[woman] What the hell is this?

51:53.652 --> 51:54.694
It seems like

51:55.570 --> 51:57.364
chess, or shogi, more like.

51:57.948 --> 52:01.701
If you get tagged when they push your
button, you're captured by the enemy team.

52:02.702 --> 52:05.789
You switch sides, you fight for them now.

52:05.872 --> 52:07.541
That's how it works.

52:07.624 --> 52:09.417
[PA chiming]

52:09.501 --> 52:13.130
Please equip your vests,
with the buttons facing the back.

52:14.256 --> 52:16.258
[muttering]

52:24.307 --> 52:26.768
- [man] I'm sure it'll be fine.
- [woman] How do you do this?

52:28.311 --> 52:29.980
Can I see yours?

52:33.233 --> 52:34.651
[siren blares]

52:34.734 --> 52:38.113
[computer] Round one.
Queen Team's turn begins.

52:38.738 --> 52:40.991
The turn will last five minutes.

52:41.575 --> 52:43.368
Game start.

52:44.870 --> 52:46.872
- [running footsteps]
- Huh?

52:51.793 --> 52:53.920
[man] They're coming.
They're coming. They're coming!

52:55.422 --> 52:56.840
They're coming for us!

52:57.799 --> 52:59.885
They'll get us all if we stay together!
Let's split up!

52:59.968 --> 53:01.011
- Yeah!
- Okay? Let's go!

53:01.094 --> 53:02.137
- Come on!
- Move!

53:02.220 --> 53:03.889
- We can't stay together!
- Hurry!

53:03.972 --> 53:04.806
- Hide!
- This way!

53:04.890 --> 53:05.849
- Go!
- Go, go!

53:05.932 --> 53:07.934
[bleeping]

53:11.605 --> 53:12.606
We'll keep you safe.

53:13.190 --> 53:14.816
Just stay right here, okay?

53:16.401 --> 53:18.195
- [Kota] Okay.
- [Arisu] Usagi, come on.

53:19.738 --> 53:21.740
[Usagi breathing shakily]

53:30.457 --> 53:32.751
[man] Go, go! Hurry! Go, go!

53:33.960 --> 53:34.961
Go!

53:35.045 --> 53:37.255
- No, they're here!
- Go back, go back! Run!

53:37.839 --> 53:39.216
[woman] Left! This way!

53:41.092 --> 53:43.678
- Keep running! They're here!
- [man] Run, run, run!

53:43.762 --> 53:45.513
No, out of the way! Out of the way!

53:45.597 --> 53:47.599
[gasping and panting]

53:50.185 --> 53:52.020
[man screaming]

53:57.400 --> 53:59.110
Oh no! [screams]

54:05.325 --> 54:06.743
- [energy buzzing]
- [screams]

54:12.499 --> 54:16.044
Pushing the button gives you
a little shock. I should have said.

54:16.127 --> 54:19.297
But don't worry,
you're gonna be my pawn next turn.

54:21.883 --> 54:23.051
[groaning]

54:25.220 --> 54:27.013
- [man 1] Where?
- [man 2] They went that way.

54:27.681 --> 54:30.016
Up! There's one up!

54:31.101 --> 54:32.143
Run!

54:33.353 --> 54:34.813
- [yelps]
- [clang]

54:37.065 --> 54:38.400
[groans]

54:39.901 --> 54:40.902
[yells]

54:41.403 --> 54:42.445
[grunts]

54:43.947 --> 54:45.865
[energy crackling]

54:49.786 --> 54:51.788
[tense, energetic music]

55:04.968 --> 55:08.722
[computer] The first turn
is ending in ten seconds.

55:08.805 --> 55:11.850
Ten, nine, eight,

55:11.933 --> 55:14.102
- seven, six…
- [Arisu] This is bad.

55:14.185 --> 55:15.645
- …five…
- [Arisu] Look at all the red.

55:15.729 --> 55:17.689
- …four, three…
- But at least her turn is up.

55:17.772 --> 55:19.024
…two, one.

55:19.107 --> 55:20.400
[siren blares]

55:20.900 --> 55:22.444
Starting the Challengers' turn.

55:24.821 --> 55:27.240
The turn will last five minutes.

55:27.741 --> 55:28.742
Turn start.

55:28.825 --> 55:31.244
- [bell rings]
- Let's get back the ones we lost.

55:31.328 --> 55:34.581
Besides, it's not like the new pawns
are gonna wanna work for her.

55:34.664 --> 55:36.082
They'll wanna rejoin us, right?

55:36.166 --> 55:38.543
- Right.
- Yeah. Okay. Let's go!

55:42.714 --> 55:44.758
[man] Hey! Hey! Over here!

55:44.841 --> 55:45.925
Up here! Up here!

55:46.009 --> 55:48.887
Hey! Come on! Get up here. Help! Help!

55:48.970 --> 55:50.096
You gotta tag me back!

55:50.680 --> 55:51.973
- Okay, hang on!
- Hurry!

55:52.474 --> 55:54.684
- Don't move!
- Hurry up! Hurry!

56:01.816 --> 56:02.692
[man] Up here!

56:03.526 --> 56:05.362
Huh? Whoa!

56:06.029 --> 56:07.030
Here, thanks!

56:07.113 --> 56:08.114
[grunts]

56:16.289 --> 56:18.041
[yelling]

56:18.541 --> 56:19.709
[gasps]

56:20.293 --> 56:21.878
What's she doing to him?

56:21.961 --> 56:23.838
She's stopping him from tagging.

56:23.922 --> 56:27.217
Of course. The rules
didn't mention anything about that.

56:28.093 --> 56:30.428
- [siren blares]
- [computer] Round three.

56:30.512 --> 56:33.056
Queen Team's turn begins.

56:33.765 --> 56:36.226
The turn will last five minutes.

56:36.309 --> 56:38.103
- Turn start.
- [bell rings]

56:38.186 --> 56:39.854
We're gonna have to split up.

56:39.938 --> 56:41.898
Get each player back one by one.

56:41.981 --> 56:44.609
If we split up,
maybe we won't find each other again.

56:44.692 --> 56:45.985
I'm not losing you.

56:51.950 --> 56:54.369
After each turn,
there's a siren that goes off.

56:54.452 --> 56:55.453
Yeah…

56:58.915 --> 57:02.502
When it does, come to this side.
We'll be able to check on each other.

57:03.169 --> 57:04.379
Right. Got it.

57:08.258 --> 57:09.968
[panting]

57:16.307 --> 57:17.934
- [Queen yells]
- [grunts]

57:18.017 --> 57:19.686
[groaning]

57:29.487 --> 57:30.905
No! Please!

57:30.989 --> 57:33.241
Stay back! Stop!

57:33.324 --> 57:34.576
[whimpering]

57:42.584 --> 57:44.210
You wanna live or not?

57:45.920 --> 57:46.754
I wanna live.

57:47.505 --> 57:49.966
Then you're gonna have to play on my team.

57:50.049 --> 57:51.342
[siren blares]

57:51.426 --> 57:54.012
[computer] Turn five.
One minute remaining.

57:56.389 --> 57:58.349
- [energy crackling]
- [groaning]

58:03.646 --> 58:04.856
[man] No, stop!

58:07.901 --> 58:10.320
You-- you get back here! Stop running!

58:10.403 --> 58:11.488
Damn it!

58:14.532 --> 58:15.450
That's it…

58:18.786 --> 58:20.788
- [energy crackling]
- [groaning]

58:26.836 --> 58:28.838
[breathing shakily]

58:44.479 --> 58:46.481
- [man whimpers]
- [woman shouts]

58:47.941 --> 58:49.943
[whoops and laughs]

58:51.653 --> 58:53.279
- Ah! Got you! Yes!
- [groans]

58:53.363 --> 58:55.240
- [energy crackling]
- [laughing]

58:58.409 --> 59:02.914
[computer] Round ten.
Challenger Team's turn begins.

59:02.997 --> 59:05.333
The turn will last five minutes.

59:05.416 --> 59:07.210
- Turn start.
- [bell rings]

59:07.794 --> 59:08.962
Let me help you!

59:12.799 --> 59:15.677
- [gasps]
- Wait! Wait. Hang on!

59:18.930 --> 59:20.682
[man whimpers]

59:26.479 --> 59:28.189
- [gasps]
- [running upstairs]

59:30.358 --> 59:32.652
- [siren blares]
- [computer] Round 11.

59:32.735 --> 59:35.196
Queen Team's turn begins.

59:35.697 --> 59:37.865
The turn will last five minutes.

59:37.949 --> 59:39.867
- Turn start.
- [bell rings]

59:39.951 --> 59:41.619
- [Arisu] You okay?
- [Usagi] Okay!

59:45.498 --> 59:47.917
- Go, run!
- Hurry up! It'll be the next turn soon!

59:48.001 --> 59:50.420
- Got you! Hah! Loser!
- [woman grunts] Oh, no!

59:54.924 --> 59:55.925
[yelling]

59:57.343 --> 59:59.345
- [energy crackling]
- [groaning]

01:00:09.355 --> 01:00:11.357
- [energy crackling]
- [groaning]

01:00:13.484 --> 01:00:15.236
Join us on the Queen's Team.

01:00:16.279 --> 01:00:18.031
[man] What? What do you mean?

01:00:19.574 --> 01:00:23.286
If you stay in this arena,
you don't have to play the other games.

01:00:23.369 --> 01:00:26.706
King of Spades can't kill you either,
if you're in here. [chuckles]

01:00:27.415 --> 01:00:28.583
That's not bad, huh?

01:00:30.001 --> 01:00:31.711
Wait, you're players too?

01:00:31.794 --> 01:00:34.172
- Just players like us?
- [man 1] Sure we are.

01:00:34.797 --> 01:00:37.634
We played this game last time
and won by sticking with the Queen.

01:00:38.718 --> 01:00:41.429
She's strong, man. She never loses.

01:00:41.512 --> 01:00:43.848
Plus if we win, we get to stay right here.

01:00:44.682 --> 01:00:48.561
So if the Queen never loses,
then her team gets to keep playing.

01:00:48.645 --> 01:00:49.520
You get it?

01:00:50.480 --> 01:00:54.233
The Queen's team gets to survive
in this place as long as they want.

01:00:55.151 --> 01:00:58.196
Pretty cool, wouldn't you say, man?

01:01:17.382 --> 01:01:19.759
- [woman] Found anyone else?
- [man] No, not yet.

01:01:19.842 --> 01:01:21.344
[woman] Let's look upstairs.

01:01:21.886 --> 01:01:23.388
[gasps] Oh, shit.

01:01:30.395 --> 01:01:31.771
It's not so bad, right?

01:01:32.397 --> 01:01:34.899
At least we don't have to die
in some other game.

01:01:36.025 --> 01:01:37.110
Yeah.

01:01:38.027 --> 01:01:41.364
Yeah, boys!
It's easy if we all work together now!

01:01:41.447 --> 01:01:43.950
Protect the Queen
and protect your own lives, all right?

01:01:44.951 --> 01:01:46.035
Yeah.

01:01:51.874 --> 01:01:53.459
[woman] I feel bad for the kid.

01:01:54.043 --> 01:01:55.378
But it's him or us, right?

01:01:56.587 --> 01:02:00.007
Exactly. There's nothing
we can do about it now.

01:02:01.884 --> 01:02:04.011
[Queen] There's only three of them left.

01:02:04.095 --> 01:02:05.096
[all gasp]

01:02:06.180 --> 01:02:07.890
[Queen] Victory is in sight.

01:02:08.766 --> 01:02:11.102
And best of all, none of you have to die.

01:02:13.354 --> 01:02:15.356
- Oh!
- But listen.

01:02:16.357 --> 01:02:18.818
I wanna get one more of them.

01:02:18.901 --> 01:02:20.194
One more? Which one?

01:02:20.862 --> 01:02:23.072
The guy who knew the girl and the kid.

01:02:24.157 --> 01:02:26.743
Oh yeah. Arisu or something.

01:02:28.411 --> 01:02:29.787
Yeah, exactly.

01:02:35.293 --> 01:02:36.461
I want him.

01:02:39.714 --> 01:02:44.177
[computer] Two more people
until checkmate. Turn 13.

01:02:44.260 --> 01:02:46.512
Starting Queen's turn.

01:02:46.596 --> 01:02:48.973
The turn will last five minutes.

01:02:49.056 --> 01:02:50.892
- Turn, start.
- [bell rings]

01:02:54.520 --> 01:02:55.813
[man] There he is!

01:03:16.834 --> 01:03:17.710
Go, run!

01:03:17.794 --> 01:03:19.003
She's after you.

01:03:19.921 --> 01:03:20.797
[Arisu] What?

01:03:32.475 --> 01:03:34.477
[theme music]
